stream
BT /F2 18 Tf 54 732 Td (LDC Chapter Setup Guide) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (This guide is for chapter operators setting up LDC for the first time. Follow the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 689 Td (  steps in order. If something fails, stop and send the exact error message to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 675 Td (  person helping you.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 649 Td (What You Are Setting Up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 624 Td (You are setting up three things:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 603 Td (1. The LDC app, where organizers manage participants and sessions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 589 Td (2. The PostgreSQL database, where the app stores records.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 575 Td (3. pgAdmin, a database viewer that lets you inspect the database in a browser.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 554 Td (You do not need to work inside the database for normal setup. Most steps are copy-) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 540 Td (  and-run commands.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 514 Td (Before You Start) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 489 Td (Ask your technical helper for:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 468 Td (- The GitHub repository link.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 454 Td (- The database name, username, and password you should use.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 440 Td (- The organizer login password for the site.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 426 Td (- The pgAdmin email and password.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 412 Td (- The SMTP/Gmail address and app password for outgoing email.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 398 Td (- The name, date, and location for your chapter's first session.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 377 Td (Do not send passwords through regular email or text if you can avoid it. Use a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 363 Td (  password manager, secure note, or phone call.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 337 Td (Open A Terminal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 312 Td (On Mac:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 291 Td (1. Open Spotlight with Command + Space.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 277 Td (2. Type Terminal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 263 Td (3. Press Enter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 242 Td (On Windows:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 221 Td (1. Install Windows Terminal if you do not already have it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 207 Td (2. Open Windows Terminal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 193 Td (3. Use the Ubuntu/Linux tab if this project was set up through WSL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 172 Td (On Linux:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 151 Td (1. Open the Terminal app.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 125 Td (Get The Code) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 100 Td (Your helper may do this part for you. If not, run:) Tj ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 54 79 Td (git clone https://github.com/NickCarreiro/LDC.git) Tj ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 54 65 Td (cd LDC) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
