17 0 obj
<< /Length 2804 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td (- Access to the AWS account where the LDC server is running.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724 Td (- Access to the domain's DNS settings. This is probably Wix.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710 Td (- The exact domain name, such as example.org.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696 Td (- A technical helper for the Nginx and HTTPS certificate steps.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 675 Td (### Step 1: Create The Permanent AWS IP Address) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 654 Td (AWS calls this an Elastic IP. It is a permanent public IP address for the server.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 633 Td (In AWS:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612 Td (1. Open the AWS Console.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 598 Td (2. Go to EC2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (3. Make sure you are in the same AWS region as the LDC server.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570 Td (4. In the left menu, click Elastic IPs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 556 Td (5. Click Allocate Elastic IP address.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 542 Td (6. Keep the normal Amazon IPv4 option.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 528 Td (7. Click Allocate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 514 Td (8. Select the new Elastic IP.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 500 Td (9. Click Actions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 486 Td (10. Click Associate Elastic IP address.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472 Td (11. Choose the LDC EC2 instance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 458 Td (12. Click Associate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 437 Td (Write down the Elastic IP address. It will look like four numbers separated by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 423 Td (  dots.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 402 Td (Important: do not leave an Elastic IP unattached. AWS can charge for unused) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 388 Td (  Elastic IPs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 367 Td (### Step 2: Make Sure The Server Allows Website Traffic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346 Td (In AWS, open the security group for the LDC server. The inbound rules should) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332 Td (  allow:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 311 Td (| Type | Port | Source |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 297 Td (| --- | --- | --- |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 283 Td (| HTTP | 80 | Anywhere |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 269 Td (| HTTPS | 443 | Anywhere |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 255 Td (| SSH | 22 | Only the helper's IP address |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 234 Td (Do not open PostgreSQL to the internet.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 213 Td (Before changing Wix, ask the helper to check:) Tj ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 54 192 Td (curl -I http://ELASTIC_IP_ADDRESS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 164 Td (Replace ELASTIC_IP_ADDRESS with the real Elastic IP.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 143 Td (### Step 3: Point The Wix Domain To AWS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 122 Td (In Wix:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 101 Td (1. Log in to Wix.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 87 Td (2. Go to Domains.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 73 Td (3. Find the chapter domain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 59 Td (4. Open the domain's Domain Actions menu.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R /F2 4 0 R /F3 5 0 R >> >> /Contents 17 0 R >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /Length 2911 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td (5. Click Manage DNS Records.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724 Td (6. Find the A record for the main domain. It may say @.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710 Td (7. Change that A record to the AWS Elastic IP.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696 Td (8. Add or update www:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682 Td (   - Use a CNAME record named www pointing to the main domain, if Wix allows it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668 Td (   - Otherwise, use an A record named www pointing to the same Elastic IP.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 654 Td (9. Save the changes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 633 Td (The records should look roughly like this:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612 Td (| Host | Type | Points To |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 598 Td (| --- | --- | --- |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (| @ | A | AWS Elastic IP |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570 Td (| www | CNAME | Main domain |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 549 Td (DNS changes may work quickly, or they may take 24-48 hours.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 528 Td (### Step 4: Finish HTTPS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 507 Td (After Wix points to AWS, the technical helper needs to configure Nginx and HTTPS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 493 Td (  on the server.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472 Td (They should make sure:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 451 Td (- The Nginx server_name includes both the main domain and www.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 437 Td (- Nginx sends website traffic to the LDC frontend service.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 423 Td (- HTTPS certificates are installed for both names.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 409 Td (- Both https://example.org and https://www.example.org load the site.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 388 Td (Do not announce the site as ready until HTTPS works.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 362 Td (Make A Backup Before Big Changes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 337 Td (Before deleting data, importing real participants, or changing session setup, make) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 323 Td (  a backup:) Tj ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 54 302 Td (pg_dump "postgresql://ldc:ldc_dev_password@localhost:5432/ldc" \\) Tj ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 54 288 Td (  --format=custom \\) Tj ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 54 274 Td (  --file "ldc-backup-$\(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S\).dump") Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 246 Td (If your .env uses a different database password or port, ask your helper for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 232 Td (  exact backup command.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 211 Td (Keep backups somewhere private. They may contain sensitive participant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 197 Td (  information.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 171 Td (What To Send Your Helper If Something Breaks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 146 Td (Send these four things:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 125 Td (1. What you were trying to do.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 111 Td (2. The command you ran.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 97 Td (3. The full error message.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 83 Td (4. A screenshot if the problem happened in the browser.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 62 Td (Do not send the .env file or database password in a group chat.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
